**12. COMPLIANCE AND AUDIT**

12.1 The Recipient shall maintain, for the duration of the Grant Period and for a period of five (5) years thereafter, complete and accurate records relating to the Project, including but not limited to:

(a) all financial records, receipts, invoices, vouchers, and bank statements evidencing the expenditure of Grant Funds;

(b) records of all income generated by or attributable to the Project, including any interest earned on Grant Funds held in a designated account;

(c) attendance records, registration forms, and participant feedback for all training sessions and activities conducted under the Project;

(d) correspondence and meeting minutes with partner organisations, volunteers, and beneficiaries;

(e) any other documents necessary to substantiate the Recipient's compliance with its obligations under this Agreement.

12.2 All records shall be maintained in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles and shall be made available to BFF, or to any auditor appointed by BFF, upon reasonable notice and during normal business hours. The Recipient shall provide access to its premises, personnel, and systems as may be reasonably required for the purpose of an audit or review.

12.3 BFF, or its authorised representatives, may conduct an audit or review of the Recipient's use of Grant Funds at any time during the Grant Period and within three (3) years after the submission of the Final Report. The Recipient shall cooperate fully with any such audit, including by providing timely responses to requests for information and documentation.

12.4 The Recipient shall procure that any sub-recipient, contractor, or third-party service provider engaged in connection with the Project complies with the requirements of this Clause 12, where applicable.

---

**13. OBLIGATIONS OF THE GRANT RECIPIENT**

13.1 The Recipient shall:

(a) implement the Project in accordance with the approved proposal and implementation plan, and achieve the outputs and outcomes described therein;

(b) use the Grant Funds solely for the purposes set out in Schedule B (Budget) and in accordance with the approved budget line items, unless a variation has been approved in writing by BFF;

(c) comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and guidelines of Singapore, including the Charities Act 1994, the Code of Governance for Charities and IPCs, and any directives issued by the Commissioner of Charities;

(d) not use Grant Funds for any political activities, religious proselytisation, or any purpose that is unlawful, unethical, or contrary to public policy;

(e) obtain all necessary permits, licences, and approvals required for the implementation of the Project;

(f) conduct its activities in a manner that respects the dignity, rights, and well-being of all beneficiaries and participants, and maintain appropriate safeguarding policies and procedures;

(g) inform BFF immediately, and in any event within seven (7) calendar days, of any matter that may materially affect the implementation of the Project or the use of Grant Funds, including any investigation, complaint, or legal proceeding involving the Recipient or its personnel;

(h) acknowledge the support of BFF in all publications, press releases, and public communications relating to the Project, using the acknowledgement guidelines provided by BFF;

(i) ensure that any intellectual property arising from the Project is managed in accordance with the terms set out in Clause 16; and

13.2 The Recipient shall ensure that all personnel involved in the Project, including volunteers, are adequately trained and briefed on the requirements of this Agreement, including the safeguarding policies referred to in Clause 13.1(f).

13.3 The Recipient shall maintain a proper filing system for all Project records, including financial records, attendance lists, and correspondence with BFF, and shall make such records available to BFF upon request.

13.4 The Recipient shall not, without the prior written consent of BFF, assign, transfer, or subcontract any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement, except as expressly permitted in the approved proposal.

---

**14. AMENDMENTS AND VARIATIONS**

14.1 Any amendment or variation to this Agreement, including any change to the Project scope, budget, implementation timeline, or key personnel, shall be made in writing and signed by both parties. No oral amendment or variation shall be effective.

14.2 The Recipient may request an amendment by submitting a completed Amendment Request Form (as set out in Schedule D) to BFF at least thirty (30) calendar days before the proposed effective date of the amendment, unless a shorter period is agreed by BFF in writing.

14.3 Each Amendment Request Form shall include:
(a) a reference to the relevant clause or schedule of this Agreement;
(b) a clear description of the proposed change and the reasons for it;
(c) an explanation of the impact of the proposed change on the Project’s outputs, outcomes, and budget;
(d) a revised budget or implementation plan, where applicable; and
(e) any supporting documents that BFF may reasonably require.

14.4 BFF shall consider each Amendment Request Form and shall respond in writing within fifteen (15) working days of receipt. BFF may:
(a) approve the amendment in whole or in part;
(b) approve the amendment subject to conditions;
(c) request further information; or
(d) decline the amendment, providing reasons in writing.

14.5 Any approved amendment shall take effect on the date stated in the written approval, or on such other date as the parties may agree in writing. The Recipient shall not implement any proposed change until it has received BFF’s written approval.

14.6 For the avoidance of doubt, the following matters shall require a formal amendment to this Agreement and may not be implemented without BFF’s prior written consent:
(a) any change to the total Grant Amount;
(b) any change to the Project’s primary objectives or target beneficiaries;
(c) any change to the Project location;
(d) any reallocation of funds between budget line items exceeding ten percent (10%) of the total Grant Amount;
(e) any change to the Project duration; and
(f) any change to the Recipient’s legal name, registered address, or authorised signatories.

14.7 Minor administrative corrections, such as typographical errors or updates to contact details, may be made by BFF unilaterally and communicated to the Recipient in writing. Such corrections shall not constitute amendments for the purposes of this Clause 14.

---

**15. TERMINATION**

15.1 BFF may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect by written notice to the Recipient if:
(a) the Recipient commits a material breach of any term of this Agreement and fails to remedy such breach within fourteen (14) calendar days of receiving written notice from BFF;
(b) the Recipient becomes insolvent, goes into liquidation, or is otherwise unable to pay its debts as they fall due;
(c) the Recipient is found to have provided false or misleading information in its application or in any report submitted under this Agreement;
(d) the Recipient fails to comply with any applicable law or regulation, including the Charities Act 1994;
(e) the Recipient uses Grant Funds for any purpose other than those permitted under this Agreement; or
(f) in BFF’s reasonable opinion, the continuation of the Project would bring BFF or the charitable sector into disrepute.
